In 6 years (and more) I have never ascended.

After the recent thread eminating from WiDTh. (and a growing respect for
rgrn) I have decided that cheating is not the way to go.  Spoilers are fine;
I already buckled anyway.  Otherwise, I could have spent a lifetime trying
to figure out some simple details.

My main purpose for cheating, after 6 years,  was merely to see what
ascending was like and what I should expect to run into.  But, now I realize
that what I originally loved about this game so much was the fact that IT
WASN'T EASY!  There are plenty of games out there where saving is a click
away.  Some good, some bad.  (I'd say I am a strong fan of Sid Meier's work;
great strategy games, lots of detail.)  But, Nethack is the only game to
which I have remained faithful since 1986.

However, the fact remains, in the 6 years since I discovered Nethack reborn
from its predecessor, Hack, I haven't ascended.  And when I see posts like
the previous ("2 in one week!") I can't help but feel a little disheartened.
I haven't even reached Rodney yet.  So the Planes, and whatever else lie
beyond are out of the question.  What am I doing wrong!?

I guess I should give some questions to get this moving in the right
direction...

1)  I have a habit of getting impatient with the tedium.  How do all of you
'ascension artists' remain patient enough to deal with things in an
effiecient and non life-threatening manner?  For example, the Valley of
Death, with its wall-2-wall monsters, could take a week to clear out if all
the messages are acknowledged.  But, as is the case with two of my hi-level,
lo-AC, hi-HP, hi-PW, etc., etc. characters, I just plow right through them.
Then I die from something stupid yet unforseen due to the fast paced plowing
(see Juiblex below).  Is it patience, or something else?

2)  I don't know how long it takes to ascend, but I am sure that it has to
happen over a period greater that one sitting.  In other words, unless
everyone else knows something I don't, a single game is too long to complete
without having to save it and come back later.  I asked the DevTeam once
about including a game history so that it would be easier to pick up where I
left off.  They told me it would be too difficult to write into the existing
code structure.  Sounds reasonable.  But how can I do this myself?  If I am
serious about a game, I keep my own record of major events -- level
branches, special levels, the tune, bulk items left behind, etc..  I have
even documented other reminders, like fountain locations, immediate goals
before I saved, as yet undefeated foes, etc..  Here is an example:

